    <h1>Ecocruceros receives an award for promoting sustainable tourism</h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">After 30 years as pioneers of marine ecotourism in Peru, Ecocruceros was recognized for its work in favor of sustainable tourism.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">This recognition celebrates a journey dedicated to bringing people closer to the wildlife of the Palomino Islands responsibly, respecting the habitat and the National Reserve.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">The recognition was granted by the <strong>International Federation of Associations of Women Tourism Executives (FIASEET)</strong>, through its Sustainable Tourism Committee (COMTUS), in the <strong>3rd Best Practices in Sustainable Tourism &amp; SDGs competition ("towards a generation of equality")</strong>. Ecocruceros earned <strong>2nd place in the Members category</strong>, in October 2024.</p>
